From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 18:29:43 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] bus: simple-pm-bus: bind T6041 PMGR register banks

T6040 describes its PMGR banks with apple,t6041-pmgr first and
apple,t8103-pmgr as a fallback. The transparent-bus probe rejects a
fallback-only match to avoid claiming devices with a dedicated driver.

Match T6041 explicitly so its register banks bind as transparent buses.
This allows the proxy fw_devlink consumers of their child power domains
to complete and releases the genpd sync_state hold through the normal
driver core path.

Exercise the production probe and match table on the host, including a
removed-match negative control and the guard against claiming unknown
specific compatibles.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Ryan Murray <ryan@aurorasilicon.org>

(backported from commit ac6ae4bf6854670b623282f7da6f00aa64ca48c5)
[j604: taken for its host test of the transparent PMGR binding, which the
 next commit extends to the T8132 match. tools/asahi/run-host-tests.py does
 not exist in this tree (the omacom base runs each tools/asahi test on its
 own), so its registration hunk is left out; run the test directly:
 python3 tools/asahi/pmgr-bus-tests.py. The match-table hunk also drops the
 stray line-continuation backslash after the T6020 entry, as upstream.]
Signed-off-by: Dylan Ironside <dylan@dylanironside.io>
Assisted-by: Claude:claude-opus-5.5

---
 drivers/bus/simple-pm-bus.c   |   3 +-
 tools/asahi/pmgr-bus-tests.py | 138 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 2 files changed, 140 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)
